                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "As Table Tennis player (casual/semi comp) \nI'd love to say that this game have extreme accurate physics to the ball. One thing bugging me though is that the racket itself, most of the time my forehand swing doesn't even lead the ball in right direction despite I swung it exactly how I do in real life, the ball in vr always seem to go so low it hit a net no matte what.\n\nGreat game though, but too bad the forehand suck most of time, I don't if it related to other's comment about racket but yup it is bad.  It may be one minor thing, but that minor thing is an essential thing in Ping Pong. \n\nI'll have to give this a 8.5/10  it would've been 10 honestly if it wasn't for forehand",
